{{- /*
  support/channel-fragment-read — read ONE topical fragment of the per-channel
  support playbook.

  Fragments live under `.mitto/support/<channel-id>/<fragment>.md`, one topic
  per file. Standard fragments: scope, tone, investigation, resources,
  escalation, redirects. Missing fragments fall back to the caller prompt's
  built-in defaults — never a hard failure.

  Owner semantics: if `OwnerAsk` is true, the fragment is owned by the calling
  prompt and the agent should ask the user (via `mitto_ui_form`) to fill it
  in when missing, then write the file. If false (reader mode), the caller
  just logs a `[CONTEXT]` note and continues with in-prompt defaults.

  Callers pass named fields via a `dict`:

      Fragment: short filename stem (no extension). One of:
                "scope" | "tone" | "investigation" | "resources"
                | "escalation" | "redirects".
      Purpose:  short caller-supplied phrase spliced into "use it to <Purpose>".
      Owner:    canonical name of the owner prompt, e.g. "Support: reply to
                user" — used in the missing-file message so the reader tells
                the user which prompt would populate it. Required.
      OwnerAsk: bool. If true, the CALLING prompt is itself the owner and
                should ask + write when the fragment is missing. If false
                (reader mode), the caller just logs a `[CONTEXT]` note and
                continues with in-prompt defaults.

  Usage (rendered as a single Markdown bullet — the CALLER supplies the
  leading `- `):

      - {{ template "_shared/support/channel-fragment-read"
           (dict "Fragment" "tone"
                 "Purpose"  "shape the tone when drafting the reply"
                 "Owner"    "Support: reply to user"
                 "OwnerAsk" false) }}

  Whitespace: fragment body starts flush at column 1 (no leading `- `) and
  emits no trailing newline; callers use plain `{{ template ... }}`.
*/ -}}
{{- $fragment := .Fragment -}}
{{- $purpose  := .Purpose  -}}
{{- $owner    := .Owner    -}}
{{- $ownerAsk := .OwnerAsk -}}
**Read the channel playbook fragment `{{ $fragment }}.md`.** Using the bead's `slack_channel`
  value, read **`.mitto/support/<channel-id>/{{ $fragment }}.md`** (e.g. `C0XXXXXXX` →
  `.mitto/support/C0XXXXXXX/{{ $fragment }}.md`). This is the **authoritative `{{ $fragment }}`
  guide** for this channel — use it to {{ $purpose }}. **If it exists**, honor its guidance; it
  **overrides** the generic defaults below.
  {{- if $ownerAsk }} **If it does not exist**, this prompt owns creating it: ask the user for
  the `{{ $fragment }}` content via a focused `mitto_ui_form`, write the file, then proceed. See
  the owner-ask step below for the field list.
  {{- else }} **If it does not exist**, log a short `[CONTEXT]` bead comment noting
  `{{ $fragment }}.md missing — using generic defaults; owner = **{{ $owner }}**` and continue
  with the generic defaults in this section. Do **not** ask the user here — only **{{ $owner }}**
  is responsible for populating this fragment.
  {{- end }}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
